\title{Arc length}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2023-01-15}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Let #{\gamma \colon [a, b] \to \mathbb{C}} be a #{C^1}-smooth curve. Then we define the \em{arc-length} of #{\gamma} to be}

##{\operatorname{length}(\gamma) := \int_a^b |\gamma'(t)|\,dt.}

\p{We say #{\gamma} is \em{simple} if #{\gamma(t_1) = \gamma(t_2) \Rightarrow t_1 = t_2} or #{\lbrace t_1, t_2\rbrace  = \lbrace a, b\rbrace }. If #{\gamma} is simple, #{\operatorname{length}(\gamma)} is the length of the image of #{\gamma}.}
